-- title:
--   Hecke's functional equation for narrow class characters
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field and let $\chi$ be a monoid homomorphism from `NarrowRayClassGroup K ⊤` to $\mathbb{C}$, that is, from the quotient of the subgroup `coprimeToModulus K ⊤` of the units of the fractional ideals of $\mathcal{O}_K$ — those $I$ with $\operatorname{count}_v(I)=0$ for every height-one prime $v$ dividing the modulus, a vacuous condition for the modulus $\top$, so that this subgroup is everything — by the subgroup generated by `narrowRaySet K ⊤`; assume $\chi \neq 1$. Let $S$ be a finite set of real places of $K$ satisfying [`M4aP2.IsParity K ⊤ χ S`](def/NumberField_RayCharacterData.html#L26): for every $\alpha \in \mathcal{O}_K$ with $\alpha \neq 0$ (the congruence $\alpha - 1 \in \top$ being automatic), the value of $\chi$ on the class of the principal fractional ideal $(\alpha)$ equals $\prod_{w \in S} \operatorname{sign}(\sigma_w(\alpha))$, the product of the signs of the real embeddings attached to the places in $S$. Then there are $W \in \mathbb{C}$, $W \neq 0$, and entire functions $\Lambda, \Lambda' : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}$ such that for all $s$ with $\operatorname{Re}(s) > 1$ one has $\Lambda(s) =$ [`M4aTorus.completedRayL K ⊤ χ S s`](def/NumberField_CompletedRayL.html#L26) and $\Lambda'(s) =$ [`M4aTorus.completedRayL K ⊤ χ̄ S s`](def/NumberField_CompletedRayL.html#L26), where $\bar\chi$ is $\chi$ followed by complex conjugation, and such that $\Lambda(1-s) = W\,\Lambda'(s)$ for every $s \in \mathbb{C}$. Here `completedRayL K 𝔣 χ S s` is $(|d_K| \cdot N\mathfrak{f})^{s/2}\,\Gamma_{\mathbb{R}}(s)^{r_1 - \#S}\,\Gamma_{\mathbb{R}}(s+1)^{\#S}\,\Gamma_{\mathbb{C}}(s)^{r_2}$ times $\sum_{C} \chi(C)\,\mathrm{rayZeta}(K,\mathfrak{f},C,s)$, the exponent $r_1 - \#S$ being truncated subtraction of natural numbers.
--
--   This is Hecke's theorem on the analytic continuation and functional equation of the $L$-series of a character of the narrow ideal class group, i.e. of a character of finite order whose conductor is supported at the archimedean places, in the shape of a pair of entire functions interpolating the completed $L$-series of $\chi$ and of $\bar\chi$ beyond the region of convergence. It feeds the corresponding statement for characters of arbitrary modulus, [`NumberField.exists_completedRayL_functionalEquation_of_primitive`](thm.html#NumberField.exists_completedRayL_functionalEquation_of_primitive).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_exists_completedRayL_functionalEquation_of_modulus_top.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NumberField_CompletedRayL
import Definitions.Def_NumberField_RayCharacterData

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open NumberField NumberField.InfinitePlace Deep.NTSupply

theorem NumberField.exists_completedRayL_functionalEquation_of_modulus_top
    (K : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (χ : NarrowRayClassGroup K (⊤ : Ideal (𝓞 K)) →* ℂ) (hχ : χ ≠ 1)
    (S : Finset {w : InfinitePlace K // w.IsReal}) (hpar : M4aP2.IsParity K ⊤ χ S) :
    ∃ (W : ℂ) (Λ Λ' : ℂ → ℂ), W ≠ 0 ∧ Differentiable ℂ Λ ∧ Differentiable ℂ Λ' ∧
      (∀ s : ℂ, 1 < s.re →
        Λ s = M4aTorus.completedRayL K ⊤ χ S s ∧
        Λ' s = M4aTorus.completedRayL K ⊤ ((starRingEnd ℂ).toMonoidHom.comp χ) S s) ∧
      (∀ s : ℂ, Λ (1 - s) = W * Λ' s) := by sorry
